msgid "Compact Paths"
msgstr "Chemins compacts"

msgid ""
"A :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` expresses the same set of paths "
"as a :class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`, but in a **factorised** form that "
"groups siblings under their shared parent. This makes the structure "
"easier to read and inspect at a glance."
msgstr ""
"Un :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` exprime le même ensemble de "
"chemins qu’un :class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`, mais sous une forme "
"**factorisée** qui regroupe les nœuds frères sous leur parent commun. La "
"structure est ainsi plus facile à lire et à examiner d’un coup d’œil."

msgid "The compact structure format"
msgstr "Le format de la structure compacte"

msgid ""
"The compact form is a Python list where each element represents a branch "
"of the dictionary tree:"
msgstr ""
"La forme compacte est une liste Python dont chaque élément représente une"
" branche de l’arbre du dictionnaire :"

msgid "A **leaf** (a node with no children) is represented by its key alone."
msgstr "Une **feuille** (un nœud sans enfant) est représentée par sa seule clé."

msgid ""
"An **internal node** (a node with children) is represented as a list "
"``[key, child1, child2, ...]``, where each child follows the same rule "
"recursively."
msgstr ""
"Un **nœud interne** (un nœud qui a des enfants) est représenté par une "
"liste ``[key, child1, child2, ...]``, où chaque enfant suit récursivement"
" la même règle."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For the dictionary ``{\"a\": {\"b\": 1, \"c\": 2}, \"d\": 3}`` the "
"compact structure is:"
msgstr ""
"Pour le dictionnaire ``{\"a\": {\"b\": 1, \"c\": 2}, \"d\": 3}``, la "
"structure compacte est :"

msgid "[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"
msgstr "[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"

msgid ""
"Reading it: ``'a'`` has two children ``'b'`` and ``'c'``; ``'d'`` is a "
"leaf."
msgstr ""
"Lecture : ``'a'`` a deux enfants, ``'b'`` et ``'c'`` ; ``'d'`` est une "
"feuille."

msgid ""
"Inside a node list, every element after the first is a child of the "
"first. A nested list is a child that has children of its own, not a group"
" of siblings: ``['a', 'b', 'c']`` is ``a`` with the two children ``b`` "
"and ``c``, while ``['a', ['b', 'c']]`` is the chain ``a``, ``b``, ``c``."
msgstr ""
"Dans une liste de nœud, chaque élément après le premier est un enfant du "
"premier. Une liste imbriquée est un enfant qui a lui-même des enfants, et"
" non un groupe de nœuds frères : ``['a', 'b', 'c']`` est ``a`` avec les "
"deux enfants ``b`` et ``c``, tandis que ``['a', ['b', 'c']]`` est la "
"chaîne ``a``, ``b``, ``c``."

msgid ""
"The full expanded paths ``['a']``, ``['a', 'b']``, ``['a', 'c']``, "
"``['d']`` can be recovered exactly from this compact form. The structure "
"built from a dictionary is the *canonical* form, and each set of paths "
"has exactly one canonical form. Other structures are accepted as input "
"and can describe the same set of paths, for instance ``['d']`` instead of"
" ``'d'`` for a leaf."
msgstr ""
"Les chemins développés ``['a']``, ``['a', 'b']``, ``['a', 'c']``, "
"``['d']`` se retrouvent exactement à partir de cette forme compacte. La "
"structure construite à partir d’un dictionnaire est la forme *canonique*,"
" et chaque ensemble de chemins a exactement une forme canonique. D’autres"
" structures sont acceptées en entrée et peuvent décrire le même ensemble "
"de chemins, par exemple ``['d']`` au lieu de ``'d'`` pour une feuille."

msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import CompactPathsView\n"
">>> view = CompactPathsView()\n"
">>> view.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c']]\n"
">>> view.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c']]\n"
">>> view.structure = [['a', ['b', 'c']]]\n"
">>> view.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b', 'c']]\n"
">>> view.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d']]\n"
">>> view.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import CompactPathsView\n"
">>> view = CompactPathsView()\n"
">>> view.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c']]\n"
">>> view.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c']]\n"
">>> view.structure = [['a', ['b', 'c']]]\n"
">>> view.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b', 'c']]\n"
">>> view.structure = [['a', 'b', 'c'], ['d']]\n"
">>> view.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid "Obtaining a compact paths view"
msgstr "Obtenir une vue des chemins compacts"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": 1, \"c\": 2}, \"d\": 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": 1, \"c\": 2}, \"d\": 3})\n"
">>> cpaths = nd.compact_paths()"

msgid "Reading the structure"
msgstr "Lire la structure"

msgid ""
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"
msgstr ""
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['a', 'b', 'c'], 'd']"

msgid "Expanding to full paths"
msgstr "Développer en chemins complets"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.expand` reconstructs all paths from "
"the compact structure:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.expand` reconstruit tous les chemins"
" à partir de la structure compacte :"

msgid ""
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid ""
"Iterating a :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` directly yields the "
"same paths, in the same order as a :class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`:"
msgstr ""
"Parcourir directement un :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` produit "
"les mêmes chemins, dans le même ordre qu’un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView` :"

msgid ""
">>> list(cpaths)\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"
msgstr ""
">>> list(cpaths)\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b'], ['a', 'c'], ['d']]"

msgid "Setting a custom structure"
msgstr "Définir une structure personnalisée"

msgid ""
"The :attr:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.structure` attribute is "
"writable. You can assign a hand-crafted compact structure and then expand"
" or analyse it:"
msgstr ""
"L’attribut :attr:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.structure` est "
"modifiable. Vous pouvez y affecter une structure compacte écrite à la "
"main, puis la développer ou l’analyser :"

msgid ""
">>> cpaths.structure = [['a', 'b']]  # only two of the original four "
"paths\n"
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b']]"
msgstr ""
">>> cpaths.structure = [['a', 'b']]  # seulement deux des quatre chemins "
"d’origine\n"
">>> cpaths.expand()\n"
"[['a'], ['a', 'b']]"

msgid ""
"You can also assign a :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` directly to "
"rebuild the structure from a different source:"
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez aussi y affecter directement un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` pour reconstruire la structure à "
"partir d’une autre source :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary({\"x\": {\"y\": 1, \"z\": 2}})\n"
">>> cpaths.structure = nd2\n"
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['x', 'y', 'z']]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary({\"x\": {\"y\": 1, \"z\": 2}})\n"
">>> cpaths.structure = nd2\n"
">>> cpaths.structure\n"
"[['x', 'y', 'z']]"

msgid "Converting between views"
msgstr "Convertir d’une vue à l’autre"

msgid "Both view classes can be converted to the other in one step:"
msgstr ""
"Chacune des deux classes de vue se convertit en l’autre en une seule "
"étape :"

msgid ""
">>> # PathsView → CompactPathsView\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> cpaths = paths.to_compact()\n"
">>> # CompactPathsView → PathsView\n"
">>> paths2 = cpaths.to_paths()\n"
">>> type(cpaths).__name__, type(paths2).__name__\n"
"('CompactPathsView', 'PathsView')"
msgstr ""
">>> # PathsView → CompactPathsView\n"
">>> paths = nd.paths()\n"
">>> cpaths = paths.to_compact()\n"
">>> # CompactPathsView → PathsView\n"
">>> paths2 = cpaths.to_paths()\n"
">>> type(cpaths).__name__, type(paths2).__name__\n"
"('CompactPathsView', 'PathsView')"

msgid "Deeper nesting example"
msgstr "Exemple d’imbrication plus profonde"

msgid "The compact format handles arbitrary depth. Given:"
msgstr "Le format compact gère une profondeur quelconque. Soit :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"europe\": {\n"
"...         \"france\": {\"capital\": \"Paris\"},\n"
"...         \"germany\": {\"capital\": \"Berlin\"},\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     \"asia\": {\"japan\": {\"capital\": \"Tokyo\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> nd.compact_paths().structure\n"
"[['europe', ['france', 'capital'], ['germany', 'capital']],\n"
" ['asia', ['japan', 'capital']]]"
msgstr ""
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"europe\": {\n"
"...         \"france\": {\"capital\": \"Paris\"},\n"
"...         \"germany\": {\"capital\": \"Berlin\"},\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     \"asia\": {\"japan\": {\"capital\": \"Tokyo\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> nd.compact_paths().structure\n"
"[['europe', ['france', 'capital'], ['germany', 'capital']],\n"
" ['asia', ['japan', 'capital']]]"

msgid ""
"Each branch is factorised: ``'europe'`` groups its two country sub-"
"branches, each of which groups its single ``'capital'`` leaf."
msgstr ""
"Chaque branche est factorisée : ``'europe'`` regroupe ses deux sous-"
"branches de pays, qui regroupent chacune leur unique feuille "
"``'capital'``."

